Z||000002||dogtired||01-10-2000||12:02 PM||||I may have responded to that other post? I don't remember???<BR>I realize our cars are old, but on the inside of the rear deck lid is a sticker on both my cars that explain the procedure. And it is a little different for the automatics than the stick. I do not remember word for word but it is something like:<BR>Ground your ECM  (YES)<BR>Start motor, obtain normal operating temperature.<BR>Set E-Brake<BR>Put car in Drive<BR>Set timing cyl #1, I think at 8 BTDC<BR>Then check timing on cyl #4<BR>Average the difference between #1 and #4.<BR>Thats all I remember off the top of my head??   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Maybe someone has a computer out by their car????    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>Good Luck!  DID I Miss Something??????||||reg||6
